From 714f34b9b0353a95556ab7526b4262ae72028eb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 01:03:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add saved-meals view to QuickMealActivity overlay
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a third icon (🍽️) to the Quick Log overlay's input row, right
of the camera. Tapping it swaps the card body to a "Your Meals" list
fed from a SharedPreferences cache that the WebView mirrors whenever
saved meals change. Each row is one tap to log — the analysis result
is built from the cached data, dropped into the existing pending-meal
queue, the local notification fires, and the activity finishes,
matching the existing barcode-log pattern.

A "+ Build New Meal" link at the bottom of the list launches the main
app with a new ACTION_BUILD_MEAL intent, which the WebView handles by
opening the in-app meal builder modal directly.

Saved-meals usage (times_logged + last_logged_at) is bumped when the
queue is drained, and the native cache is re-pushed so the overlay's
most-used ordering stays current.

https://claude.ai/code/session_01YJ2nj4Hv3ZYhjKrXLJFLri
